	(title_block
		(title "Dual-mode servo port: RS-485 or TTL front-end + port power")
		(rev "A")
		(comment 1 "Sheet 12/13/14/15 — see HARDWARE.md §8, FUNCTIONAL.md")
	)
	(lib_symbols)
	(text "SERVO PORT — one sheet, instantiated 4× as servo-port-0..3. Contains everything replicated per port:\n  front-end: SP3485EN C8963 (DI=TXD, DE=TNOW, R̄E̅=TNOW when RS-485 selected) + SN74LVC2G241 C10430 (2A=TXD, 2OE=TNOW, 1OE̅=TNOW when TTL selected, 1Y=RXD)\n  mode select (D2): jumper / solder bridge routes TNOW to exactly ONE receiver enable; the other is tied inactive. Both receiver outputs wire-OR onto RXD (10 kΩ pull-up).\n  RS-485 side: A/B → J4-pin B4B-EH-A C160258 (1 GND, 2 VDD, 3 D+, 4 D−), SM712 C7420375, 120 Ω termination as 0 Ω option, +12V_SERVO → TPS16630 e-fuse C1849461 → ≥470 µF → SMBJ13A → VDD_485\n  TTL side: DATA → J3-pin B3B-EH-A C160259 (1 GND, 2 VDD, 3 DATA), 10 kΩ pull-up to +3V3, 10–22 Ω series, 5 V-working TVS, +5V_SERVO → TPS25961 e-fuse C5571272 → ≥470 µF → SMBJ6.0A → VDD_TTL\nGolden reference: datasheets/reference/robotis/dynamixel-x-ttl-circuit-3v3-74lvc2g241.png, dynamixel-x-rs485-circuit.jpg, connector pinout PNGs\nNet names the project patterns key on: A, B → RS485; DATA → TTL_DATA; VDD_485, VDD_TTL → PWR_SERVO.\nPer-instance differences are impossible (values/DNP shared) — the mode default is one choice for all four ports.\nOpen items: D1, D2, D3 (e-fuse latch/retry, GPIO enable), V1.  Consumes: +12V_SERVO, +5V_SERVO, +3V3, GND.  Test points: TXD RXD TNOW A B DATA."
